{ chrom_cmp.fox - tunes and their expansion in the energy parameter, OV NO 2 1 + TP MU.
  Variants: (FD,FQ) = (0,0) FR0 | (3,0) dipoles | (0,3) quads | (3,3) whole ring (sextupoles always FR 0)
  for GAP = 0.05, 0.025, 0.0125, 0.00625 m (half aperture).
  Output output/cosy_mu_series.csv : FD,FQ,GAP,k,MUx_k,MUy_k where MU_k = MU|(0&0&0&0&k) is the
  Taylor coefficient of the fractional tune in COSY's 5th variable dK/K (NOT dp/p, NOT a derivative):
  MU(dK) = sum_k MU_k dK^k. Conversion to delta = dp/p is done in the notebook. }
INCLUDE 'lattice_cmp';
PROCEDURE RUN;
  VARIABLE MU 1000 2; VARIABLE I 1; VARIABLE J 1; VARIABLE K 1; VARIABLE NO 1;
  VARIABLE KD 1 4; VARIABLE KQ 1 4; VARIABLE KG 1 4; VARIABLE E 1 5;
  NO := 7; OV NO 2 1;
  KD(1):=0; KQ(1):=0;  KD(2):=3; KQ(2):=0;  KD(3):=0; KQ(3):=3;  KD(4):=3; KQ(4):=3;
  KG(1):=0.05; KG(2):=0.025; KG(3):=0.0125; KG(4):=0.00625;
  OPENF 20 'output/cosy_mu_series.csv' 'UNKNOWN';
  WRITE 20 'FD,FQ,GAP,k,MUx_k,MUy_k';
  LOOP I 1 4; LOOP J 1 4;
    PART 270*PARA(1); RINGFC KD(I) KQ(I) KG(J); TP MU;
    LOOP K 0 NO-1;
      E(1):=0; E(2):=0; E(3):=0; E(4):=0; E(5):=K;
      WRITE 20 ST(KD(I))&','&ST(KQ(I))&','&ST(KG(J))&','&ST(K)&','&ST(MU(1)|(0&0&0&0&K))&','&ST(MU(2)|(0&0&0&0&K));
    ENDLOOP;
  ENDLOOP; ENDLOOP;
  CLOSEF 20;
ENDPROCEDURE;
RUN; END;
